# The OpenSCAD build the visual regression check renders with.
#
# A dated development snapshot rather than a numbered release: the last
# numbered stable is 2021.01, which predates the Manifold backend and headless
# EGL rendering, both of which this check depends on.
#
# Pinning is for reproducibility rather than correctness — before and after are
# rendered by the same binary in the same job, so a version change moves both
# sides together and cannot show up as a geometry difference.
#
# To bump: pick a snapshot from https://files.openscad.org/snapshots/, put its
# date here, and take SHA256 from the matching .sha256 file on that page.
OPENSCAD_SNAPSHOT=2026.08.13
OPENSCAD_SHA256=fed864ab17a2d9f0ddcf55eb7481865b1014b16408b7e3973e9b41c834ae6f8b
